{"id":"n1-007","title":"A というか B というか","romaji":"A to iu ka B to iu ka","jlptLevel":1,"shortExplanation":"Means 'rather than say A, it's more like B', or 'whether to call it A or B'.","longExplanation":"The grammar 'A というか B というか' is used when the speaker isn't sure which expression (A or B) describes the situation better. It can be translated as 'rather than A, it's more B' or 'should I call it A or B?'.","formation":"Phrase A + というか + Phrase B + というか","examples":[{"jp":"彼は無礼というか、直接的というか、とにかくはっきりしている。","romaji":"Kare wa burei to iu ka, chokusetsuteki to iu ka, tonikaku hakkiri shite iru.","en":"He's rather rude, or maybe just direct; in any case, he is very blunt.","words":[{"surface":"彼","vocabId":"1483070","reading":"かれ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"無礼","vocabId":"1531060","reading":"ぶれい"},{"surface":"と","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いう","vocabId":"1587040","reading":"いう"},{"surface":"か","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"直接的","vocabId":"1431250","reading":"ちょくせつてき"},{"surface":"と","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いう","vocabId":"1587040","reading":"いう"},{"surface":"か","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"とにかく","vocabId":null},{"surface":"はっきり","vocabId":null},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いる","vocabId":"1577980","reading":"いる"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[3,4,5,8,9,10]},{"jp":"この映画は面白いというか、変というか、とにかく不思議な雰囲気がある。","romaji":"Kono eiga wa omoshiroi to iu ka, hen to iu ka, tonikaku fushigi na fun'iki ga aru.","en":"This movie is interesting or maybe strange; anyway, it has a mysterious vibe.","words":[{"surface":"この","vocabId":null},{"surface":"映画","vocabId":"1173720","reading":"えいが"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"面白い","vocabId":"1533580","reading":"おもしろい"},{"surface":"と","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いう","vocabId":"1587040","reading":"いう"},{"surface":"か","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null}